{
  "comment": "Curated stingers (StingerCuration): what a net deck's Hit 1–4 fire, chosen from the track's genre and sound palette instead of the composer's fixed stinger set. `families` sorts beats' genres into genre families. `slots` gives each Hit (1–4) the candidate kinds it draws from, in order of preference: the first kind with an eligible candidate wins, and a Hit with none plays as before (its stinger net, voiced by the palette). A candidate is eligible when its `families` holds the track's family (or `*`), its `palettes` the track's palette (or `*`; no palette is `studio`), the track's tempo is inside `tempo` [min, max] BPM, its key fits (`key`: `any` = unpitched, always fits; `tonal` = pitched on the stinger nets' note 60, fits a scale that holds that pitch class), and what it plays is on this Mac. Candidates naming the track's family or palette outright weigh double in the draw, which is seeded by the track seed + Hit (`StingerCuration.resolve`), so the same configuration always gets the same hits. Kinds: `oneShot` plays `option` (SoundPalette option grammar: synth:<instrument>, gm:<program>, cat:<category>, dls:<program>, bank:<category>) on the Hit's stinger net, for `bars` (default 1); `macro` fires a NetMacro or MasterMacro by its beats id for `bars` (default: the macro's own); `loop` launches a clip on the loop row, in the deck's time, from its top, once (at most `maxBeats` beats): `stock` = an installed Apple Loop matching `category` and every word of `query`, tempo within `tempoTolerance` (relative, half and double time count) of the track's (local-only: never in a share, a session's row or the CDN), or `clip` = a loop-library clip id.",
